Mike Piff writes on the subject of writing visual markup like \it in
math mode:

 > Oh dear! Our maths school has lots of users who type their LaTeX like this.
 > They read the Get-By-In-LaTeX guide and never read any further. (And I am
 > guilty of it myself too!)
 >
 > I am rather glad now that I *didn't* notice the announcement of NFSS2. I
 > could inadvertently have inflicted it on about fifty users...

Just to make this clear: LaTeX2e will deal with this problem in a
rather simple manner: if the document uses \documentstyle, the system
will fall back to LaTeX2.09 compatibility mode. The only thing that
will not work are style files which use internal font selection
commands of the old lfonts.tex, like \tenrm.

To have the new features, you have to write \documentclass instead.


